5 & { - 1} \cr

} } \right]$$, then AB is equal
to :

questions.questionHtml:
If A is a symmetric matrix and B is a skew-symmetric matrix such that A + B = $$\left[ {\matrix{
   2 &amp; 3  \cr 
   5 &amp; { - 1}  \cr 

 } } \right]$$, then AB is equal
to :

questions.explanationText:
$$A + B = \left[ {\matrix{
2 & 3 \cr
5 & { - 1} \cr

} } \right] = P(say)$$

Now $$A = {{P + {P^T}} \over 2}\& B = {{P - {P^T}} \over 2}$$

So $$A = {1 \over 2}\left( {\left[ {\matrix{
2 & 3 \cr
5 & { - 1} \cr

} } \right] + \left[ {\matrix{
2 & 5 \cr
3 & { - 1} \cr

} } \right]} \right) = \left[ {\matrix{
2 & 4 \cr
4 & { - 1} \cr

} } \right]$$

$$B = {1 \over 2}\left( {\left[ {\matrix{
2 & 3 \cr
5 & { - 1} \cr

} } \right] - \left[ {\matrix{
2 & 5 \cr
3 & { - 1} \cr

} } \right]} \right) = \left[ {\matrix{
0 & { - 1} \cr
1 & 0 \cr

} } \right]$$

So $$AB = \left( {\left[ {\matrix{
2 & 4 \cr
4 & { - 1} \cr

} } \right]\left[ {\matrix{
0 & { - 1} \cr
1 & 0 \cr

} } \right]} \right) = \left[ {\matrix{
4 & { - 2} \cr
{ - 1} & { - 4} \cr

} } \right]$$

